DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These interfaces may be used to look up information from the
     audit_class(5) database, which describes audit event classes.  Audit
     event classes are described by _s_t_r_u_c_t _a_u___c_l_a_s_s___e_n_t.

     The ggeettaauuccllaasssseenntt() function will return the next class found in the
     audit_class(5) database, or the first if the function has not yet been
     called.  NULL will be returned if no further records are available.

     The ggeettaauuccllaassssnnaamm() function looks up a class by name.  NULL will be re‐
     turned if no matching class can be found.

     The sseettaauuccllaassss() function resets the iterator through the audit_class(5)
     database, causing the next call to ggeettaauuccllaasssseenntt() to start again from
     the beginning of the file.

     The eennddaauuccllaassss() function closes the audit_class(5) database, if open.

